IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc2-incapacity`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4.
-- LAYER 1, part ssc2, module 6 of 6: ss 40, 41 and 42 (long-term incapacity benefit for widows and widowers,
-- and entitlement after a period of employment or training for work).
-- Source: inputs/ukpga-1992-4.txt, a plain-text rendering made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text".
-- Money is a NUMBER in pounds; a rate is weekly unless the name says otherwise.
-- JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE is the Act answering in its own words; NOTHING is "not covered".
-- "The time" when a husband or wife dies is a day in these functions; "after that time" is a later day.
-- Whether a person is incapable of work is s 171A(1)'s answer (seam S35), as in ssc2-incapacity.

§ `Part II -- Long-term incapacity benefit for widows and widowers (ss 40, 41, 42)`

§§ `s 40 Long-term incapacity benefit for widows`

-- Kleene negation, "and" and "or" over MAYBE BOOLEAN: a limb the text answers "no" decides the whole even
-- when another limb is unknown; otherwise an unknown limb leaves the whole unknown.
-- src:1171 | (1) Subject to subsection (2) below, this section applies to a woman who—
-- src:1172 | (a) on her late husband’s death is not entitled to a widowed mother’s allowance or subsequently ceases to be entitled to such an allowance;
-- src:1173 | (b) is incapable of work at the time when he dies or when she subsequently ceases to be so entitled;
-- src:1174 | (c) either—
-- src:1175 | (i) would have been entitled to a widow’s pension if she had been over the age of 45 when her husband died or when she ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother’s allowance; or
-- src:1176 | (ii) is entitled to such a pension with a reduction under section 39(4) above; and
-- src:1177 | (d) is not entitled to incapacity benefit apart from this section.
@ref s 40(1) (src:1171-1177)
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40 not` MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

@ref s 40(1) (src:1171-1177)
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40 both` MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN b
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER b
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref s 40(1) (src:1171-1177)
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40 either` MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN b
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER b
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- (2) This section does not apply to a woman unless (a) her husband died after 5th April 1979; or (b) she
-- ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance after that date (whenever her husband died).
-- src:1178 | (2) This section does not apply to a woman unless—
-- src:1179 | (a) her husband died after 5th April 1979; or
-- src:1180 | (b) she ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother’s allowance after that date (whenever her husband died).
@ref s 40(2) (src:1178-1180)
GIVEN `the day on which her husband died` IS A DATE
      `the day on which she ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40(2) the section is not excluded by subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `the day on which her husband died` ABOVE (Date 5 4 1979)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the day on which she ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance`
         WHEN JUST ceased THEN (IF ceased ABOVE (Date 5 4 1979) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply to a woman unless—"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE                                                                -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply to a woman unless—"

-- (1) Subject to (2), this section applies to a woman who (a) on her late husband's death is not entitled to a
-- widowed mother's allowance or subsequently ceases to be entitled to such an allowance; (b) is incapable of
-- work at the time when he dies or when she subsequently ceases to be so entitled; (c) either (i) would have
-- been entitled to a widow's pension if she had been over the age of 45 when her husband died or when she
-- ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance, or (ii) is entitled to such a pension with a
-- reduction under s 39(4); and (d) is not entitled to incapacity benefit apart from this section.
-- src:1171 | (1) Subject to subsection (2) below, this section applies to a woman who—
-- src:1172 | (a) on her late husband’s death is not entitled to a widowed mother’s allowance or subsequently ceases to be entitled to such an allowance;
-- src:1173 | (b) is incapable of work at the time when he dies or when she subsequently ceases to be so entitled;
-- src:1174 | (c) either—
-- src:1175 | (i) would have been entitled to a widow’s pension if she had been over the age of 45 when her husband died or when she ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother’s allowance; or
-- src:1176 | (ii) is entitled to such a pension with a reduction under section 39(4) above; and
-- src:1177 | (d) is not entitled to incapacity benefit apart from this section.
@ref s 40(1) (src:1171-1177)
GIVEN `s 40(2) the section is not excluded by subsection (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `on her late husband's death she is not entitled to a widowed mother's allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `she subsequently ceases to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 171A(1) the person is incapable of work` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 38(1) the woman would have been entitled to a widow's pension if she had been over the age of 45 when her husband died or when she ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 39(4) the woman is entitled to a widow's pension with a reduction under subsection (4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the woman is entitled to incapacity benefit apart from this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40(1) the section applies to the woman` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 40(2) the section is not excluded by subsection (2)`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply to a woman unless—"
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER
            `s 40 both` (JUST (`on her late husband's death she is not entitled to a widowed mother's allowance` OR `she subsequently ceases to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance`))
                (`s 40 both` `s 171A(1) the person is incapable of work`
                    (`s 40 both`
                        (`s 40 either` `s 38(1) the woman would have been entitled to a widow's pension if she had been over the age of 45 when her husband died or when she ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance` `s 39(4) the woman is entitled to a widow's pension with a reduction under subsection (4)`)
                        (JUST (NOT `the woman is entitled to incapacity benefit apart from this section`))))
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "this section applies to a woman who—" (a) to (d)

-- (3) A woman to whom this section applies is entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under this section for
-- any day of incapacity for work which (a) falls in a period of incapacity for work that began before the time
-- when her late husband died or she subsequently ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance, and (b)
-- is after that time and after the first 364 days of incapacity for work in that period.
-- "The time" is read as a day: a period began before it only on an earlier date, and a day is after it only on a later date (fork F20 in NOTES.md).
-- src:1181 | (3) A woman to whom this section applies is entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under this section for any day of incapacity for work which—
-- src:1182 | (a) falls in a period of incapacity for work that began before the time when her late husband died or she subsequently ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother’s allowance; and
-- src:1183 | (b) is after that time and after the first 364 days of incapacity for work in that period.
@ref s 40(3) (src:1181-1183)
GIVEN `s 40(1) the section applies to the woman` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 30C(1) the relevant day is a day of incapacity for work forming part of a period of incapacity for work` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the day` IS A DATE
      `the time when her late husband died or she subsequently ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the period of incapacity for work in which the day falls` IS A DATE
      `the number of the day in the period of incapacity for work, counting the first day as 1` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40(3) the woman is entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under this section for the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 40 both` `s 40(1) the section applies to the woman` `s 30C(1) the relevant day is a day of incapacity for work forming part of a period of incapacity for work`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF (`the first day of the period of incapacity for work in which the day falls` BELOW `the time when her late husband died or she subsequently ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance`)
           AND (`the day` ABOVE `the time when her late husband died or she subsequently ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance`)
           AND (`the number of the day in the period of incapacity for work, counting the first day as 1` ABOVE 364)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for any day of incapacity for work which (a) ... and (b) ..."
    OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A woman to whom this section applies is entitled ... for any day of incapacity for work which"

-- (4) terminally ill: she suffers from a progressive disease and her death in consequence can reasonably be
-- expected within 6 months.
-- src:1187 | For the purposes of this subsection a woman is terminally ill if she suffers from a progressive disease and her death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected within 6 months.
@ref s 40(4) (src:1187)
GIVEN `the woman suffers from a progressive disease` IS A BOOLEAN
      `her death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected within 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40(4) the woman is terminally ill` MEANS
    IF `the woman suffers from a progressive disease` AND `her death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected within 6 months`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a woman is terminally ill if she suffers from a progressive disease and her death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected within 6 months"

-- (4) "who is not entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under subsection (3)": (3) is a grant, so a woman
-- (3) does not entitle is not entitled under it. NOTHING from (3) therefore counts as "not entitled" here
-- (marginal reading in NOTES.md); an unknown fact in (3) is carried by the other limbs of (4) instead.
-- src:1184 | (4) A woman to whom this section applies who is not entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under subsection (3) above, but who is terminally ill, is entitled to short-term incapacity benefit under this section for any day of incapacity for work which—
@ref s 40(4) (src:1184)
GIVEN `s 40(3) the woman is entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under this section for the day` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40(4) the woman is not entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under subsection (3)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 40(3) the woman is entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under this section for the day`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE     -- she is entitled under (3)
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE                -- (3) does not entitle her

-- (4) A woman to whom this section applies who is not entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under (3) but
-- who is terminally ill is entitled to short-term incapacity benefit under this section for any day of
-- incapacity for work which (a) falls in a period that began before the time (as in (3)) and (b) is after that
-- time and after the first 196 days of incapacity for work in that period.
-- "The time" is read as a day: a period began before it only on an earlier date, and a day is after it only on a later date (fork F20 in NOTES.md).
-- src:1184 | (4) A woman to whom this section applies who is not entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under subsection (3) above, but who is terminally ill, is entitled to short-term incapacity benefit under this section for any day of incapacity for work which—
-- src:1185 | (a) falls in a period of incapacity for work that began before the time when her late husband died or she subsequently ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother’s allowance, and
-- src:1186 | (b) is after that time and after the first 196 days of incapacity for work in that period.
@ref s 40(4) (src:1184-1186)
GIVEN `s 40(1) the section applies to the woman` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 40(4) the woman is not entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under subsection (3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 40(4) the woman is terminally ill` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 30C(1) the relevant day is a day of incapacity for work forming part of a period of incapacity for work` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the day` IS A DATE
      `the time when her late husband died or she subsequently ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the period of incapacity for work in which the day falls` IS A DATE
      `the number of the day in the period of incapacity for work, counting the first day as 1` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40(4) the woman is entitled to short-term incapacity benefit under this section for the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 40 both` `s 40(1) the section applies to the woman`
                (`s 40 both` `s 40(4) the woman is not entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under subsection (3)`
                    (`s 40 both` `s 40(4) the woman is terminally ill` `s 30C(1) the relevant day is a day of incapacity for work forming part of a period of incapacity for work`))
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF (`the first day of the period of incapacity for work in which the day falls` BELOW `the time when her late husband died or she subsequently ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance`)
           AND (`the day` ABOVE `the time when her late husband died or she subsequently ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance`)
           AND (`the number of the day in the period of incapacity for work, counting the first day as 1` ABOVE 196)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for any day of incapacity for work which (a) ... and (b) ..."
    OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A woman to whom this section applies who is not entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under subsection (3) above, but who is terminally ill, is entitled"

-- (5) The weekly rate of incapacity benefit payable under this section is (a) if the woman is not entitled to
-- a widow's pension, that which would apply if she were entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under s 30A;
-- and (b) if she is entitled to a widow's pension with a reduction under s 39(4), the difference between the
-- weekly rate of that pension and the weekly rate referred to in (a). "The difference between" two rates is
-- taken as the amount by which they differ, whichever is larger (fork F19 in NOTES.md).
-- src:1188 | (5) The weekly rate of incapacity benefit payable under this section is—
-- src:1189 | (a) if the woman is not entitled to a widow’s pension, that which would apply if she were entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under section 30A above; and
-- src:1190 | (b) if she is entitled to a widow’s pension with a reduction under section 39(4) above, the difference between the weekly rate of that pension and the weekly rate referred to in paragraph (a) above.
@ref s 40(5) (src:1188-1190)
GIVEN `the woman is entitled to a widow's pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the woman is entitled to a widow's pension with a reduction under section 39(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 30B(6) the weekly rate of long-term incapacity benefit` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `s 38 the weekly rate of that pension in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 40(5) the weekly rate of incapacity benefit payable under this section` MEANS
    IF NOT `the woman is entitled to a widow's pension`
    THEN `s 30B(6) the weekly rate of long-term incapacity benefit`     -- (a); NOTHING when the Schedule 4 figure is absent: NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Schedule 4 is omitted from this text
    ELSE IF `the woman is entitled to a widow's pension with a reduction under section 39(4)`
         THEN (CONSIDER `s 30B(6) the weekly rate of long-term incapacity benefit`
               WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Schedule 4 is omitted from this text
               WHEN JUST longTerm THEN
                   CONSIDER `s 38 the weekly rate of that pension in pounds`
                   WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the rate of the pension is worked out under sections 39 and 44 to 45B
                   WHEN JUST pension THEN JUST (IF pension ABOVE longTerm THEN pension MINUS longTerm ELSE longTerm MINUS pension))     -- (b)
         ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): (a) is for a woman not entitled to a widow's pension, (b) for one entitled with a reduction

-- (6) A woman is not entitled to incapacity benefit under this section if she is over pensionable age; but if
-- she has attained pensionable age and the period of incapacity for work mentioned in (3)(a) or (4)(a) did not
-- terminate before she attained that age (a) she shall, if not otherwise entitled to a Category A retirement
-- pension, be entitled to such a pension, and (b) the weekly rate of the Category A retirement pension to which
-- she is entitled shall be determined in the prescribed manner.
-- src:1191 | (6) A woman is not entitled to incapacity benefit under this section if she is over pensionable age; but if she has attained pensionable age and the period of incapacity for work mentioned in subsection (3)(a) or (4)(a) above did not terminate before she attained that age—
@ref s 40(6) (src:1191)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `the woman` IS A Person
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40(6) the woman is entitled to incapacity benefit under this section on the day` MEANS
    IF `the day` AT LEAST (`the woman`'s `date of attaining pensionable age`)
    THEN JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A woman is not entitled to incapacity benefit under this section if she is over pensionable age"
    ELSE NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says only when she is not entitled

-- src:1192 | (a) she shall, if not otherwise entitled to a Category A retirement pension, be entitled to such a pension, and
@ref s 40(6) (src:1192)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `the woman` IS A Person
      `the period of incapacity for work mentioned in subsection (3)(a) or (4)(a) did not terminate before she attained pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40(6)(a) the woman is entitled to a Category A retirement pension` MEANS
    IF (`the day` AT LEAST (`the woman`'s `date of attaining pensionable age`))
       AND `the period of incapacity for work mentioned in subsection (3)(a) or (4)(a) did not terminate before she attained pensionable age`
    THEN JUST TRUE     -- the subsection grants the pension "if not otherwise entitled"; she is entitled either way
    ELSE NOTHING       -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if she has attained pensionable age and the period of incapacity for work ... did not terminate before she attained that age"

-- src:1193 | (b) the weekly rate of the Category A retirement pension to which she is entitled (whether by virtue of paragraph (a) above or otherwise) shall be determined in the prescribed manner.
@ref s 40(6) (src:1193)
GIVEN `the weekly rate of the Category A retirement pension determined in the prescribed manner in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 40(6)(b) the weekly rate of the Category A retirement pension in pounds` MEANS
    `the weekly rate of the Category A retirement pension determined in the prescribed manner in pounds`     -- NOTHING when not supplied: NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "determined in the prescribed manner"

-- (7) Where a woman entitled to short-term incapacity benefit under (4) attains pensionable age and defers her
-- entitlement to a Category A pension or makes an election under s 54(1), the days of incapacity for work in the
-- period mentioned in (4) are treated, for determining any subsequent entitlement to incapacity benefit under
-- s 30A or its rate, as days of entitlement to short-term incapacity benefit. The number of days to add to
-- s 30D's count is the answer.
-- src:1194 | (7) Where a woman entitled to short-term incapacity benefit under subsection (4) above attains pensionable age and defers her entitlement to a Category A pension or makes an election under section 54(1) below, the days of incapacity for work falling within the period of incapacity for work mentioned in that subsection shall, for the purpose of determining any subsequent entitlement to incapacity benefit under section 30A above or the rate of that benefit, be treated as if they had been days of entitlement to short-term incapacity benefit.
@ref s 40(7) (src:1194)
GIVEN `she was entitled to short-term incapacity benefit under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `she attains pensionable age and defers her entitlement to a Category A pension or makes an election under section 54(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days of incapacity for work falling within the period of incapacity for work mentioned in subsection (4)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 40(7) the number of days treated as days of entitlement to short-term incapacity benefit` MEANS
    IF `she was entitled to short-term incapacity benefit under subsection (4)` AND `she attains pensionable age and defers her entitlement to a Category A pension or makes an election under section 54(1)`
    THEN JUST `the number of days of incapacity for work falling within the period of incapacity for work mentioned in subsection (4)`
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a woman entitled to short-term incapacity benefit under subsection (4) above attains pensionable age and defers ..."

-- (8) References to short-term incapacity benefit at the higher rate include short-term incapacity benefit
-- payable under (4).
-- src:1195 | (8) References to short-term incapacity benefit at the higher rate shall be construed as including short-term incapacity benefit payable under subsection (4) above.
@ref s 40(8) (src:1195)
GIVEN `the benefit is short-term incapacity benefit payable under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40(8) the short-term incapacity benefit is at the higher rate` MEANS
    IF `the benefit is short-term incapacity benefit payable under subsection (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "shall be construed as including" does not say that other benefit is not at the higher rate

§§ `s 41 Long-term incapacity benefit for widowers`

-- (1) This section applies to a man whose wife has died on or after 6th April 1979 and who either (a) was
-- incapable of work at the time when she died, or (b) becomes incapable of work within the prescribed period
-- after that time, and is not entitled to incapacity benefit apart from this section.
-- src:1197 | (1) This section applies to a man whose wife has died on or after 6th April 1979 and who either—
-- src:1198 | (a) was incapable of work at the time when she died, or
-- src:1199 | (b) becomes incapable of work within the prescribed period after that time,
-- src:1200 | and is not entitled to incapacity benefit apart from this section.
@ref s 41(1) (src:1197-1200)
GIVEN `the day on which his wife died` IS A DATE
      `s 171A(1) the person is incapable of work` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `he becomes incapable of work within the prescribed period after that time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the man is entitled to incapacity benefit apart from this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(1) the section applies to the man` MEANS
    IF `the day on which his wife died` AT LEAST (Date 6 4 1979)
    THEN (CONSIDER `s 40 both` (`s 40 either` `s 171A(1) the person is incapable of work` (JUST `he becomes incapable of work within the prescribed period after that time`)) (JUST (NOT `the man is entitled to incapacity benefit apart from this section`))
          WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
          OTHERWISE NOTHING)     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to a man whose wife has died on or after 6th April 1979 and who either— ... and is not entitled to incapacity benefit apart from this section."
    ELSE NOTHING                 -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to a man whose wife has died on or after 6th April 1979"

-- (2) A man to whom this section applies is entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under this section for any
-- day of incapacity for work which (a) falls in a period of incapacity for work that began before the time when
-- his wife died or within the prescribed period after that time, and (b) is after that time and after the first
-- 364 days of incapacity for work in that period.
-- "The time" is read as a day: a period began before it only on an earlier date, and a day is after it only on a later date (fork F20 in NOTES.md).
-- src:1201 | (2) A man to whom this section applies is entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under this section for any day of incapacity for work which—
-- src:1202 | (a) falls in a period of incapacity for work that began before the time when his wife died or within the prescribed period after that time, and
-- src:1203 | (b) is after that time and after the first 364 days of incapacity for work in that period.
@ref s 41(2) (src:1201-1203)
GIVEN `s 41(1) the section applies to the man` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 30C(1) the relevant day is a day of incapacity for work forming part of a period of incapacity for work` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the period of incapacity for work began before the time when his wife died or within the prescribed period after that time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day` IS A DATE
      `the day on which his wife died` IS A DATE
      `the number of the day in the period of incapacity for work, counting the first day as 1` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(2) the man is entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under this section for the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 40 both` `s 41(1) the section applies to the man` `s 30C(1) the relevant day is a day of incapacity for work forming part of a period of incapacity for work`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the period of incapacity for work began before the time when his wife died or within the prescribed period after that time`
           AND (`the day` ABOVE `the day on which his wife died`)
           AND (`the number of the day in the period of incapacity for work, counting the first day as 1` ABOVE 364)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for any day of incapacity for work which (a) ... and (b) ..."
    OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A man to whom this section applies is entitled ... for any day of incapacity for work which"

-- (3) terminally ill: he suffers from a progressive disease and his death in consequence can reasonably be
-- expected within 6 months.
-- src:1207 | For the purposes of this subsection a man is terminally ill if he suffers from a progressive disease and his death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected within 6 months.
@ref s 41(3) (src:1207)
GIVEN `the man suffers from a progressive disease` IS A BOOLEAN
      `his death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected within 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(3) the man is terminally ill` MEANS
    IF `the man suffers from a progressive disease` AND `his death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected within 6 months`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a man is terminally ill if he suffers from a progressive disease and his death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected within 6 months"

-- (3) "who is not entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under subsection (2)": as in s 40(4), a man (2) does
-- not entitle is not entitled under it, so NOTHING from (2) counts as "not entitled" here.
-- src:1204 | (3) A man to whom this section applies who is not entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under subsection (2) above, but who is terminally ill, is entitled to short-term incapacity benefit under this section for any day of incapacity for work which—
@ref s 41(3) (src:1204)
GIVEN `s 41(2) the man is entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under this section for the day` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(3) the man is not entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under subsection (2)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 41(2) the man is entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under this section for the day`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE     -- he is entitled under (2)
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE                -- (2) does not entitle him

-- (3) A man to whom this section applies who is not entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under (2) but who
-- is terminally ill is entitled to short-term incapacity benefit under this section for any day of incapacity
-- for work which (a) falls in a period that began before the time when his wife died or within the prescribed
-- period after that time, and (b) is after that time and after the first 196 days in that period.
-- "The time" is read as a day: a period began before it only on an earlier date, and a day is after it only on a later date (fork F20 in NOTES.md).
-- src:1204 | (3) A man to whom this section applies who is not entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under subsection (2) above, but who is terminally ill, is entitled to short-term incapacity benefit under this section for any day of incapacity for work which—
-- src:1205 | (a) falls in a period of incapacity for work that began before the time when his wife died or within the prescribed period after that time, and
-- src:1206 | (b) is after that time and after the first 196 days of incapacity for work in that period.
@ref s 41(3) (src:1204-1206)
GIVEN `s 41(1) the section applies to the man` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 41(3) the man is not entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under subsection (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 41(3) the man is terminally ill` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 30C(1) the relevant day is a day of incapacity for work forming part of a period of incapacity for work` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the period of incapacity for work began before the time when his wife died or within the prescribed period after that time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day` IS A DATE
      `the day on which his wife died` IS A DATE
      `the number of the day in the period of incapacity for work, counting the first day as 1` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(3) the man is entitled to short-term incapacity benefit under this section for the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 40 both` `s 41(1) the section applies to the man`
                (`s 40 both` `s 41(3) the man is not entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under subsection (2)`
                    (`s 40 both` `s 41(3) the man is terminally ill` `s 30C(1) the relevant day is a day of incapacity for work forming part of a period of incapacity for work`))
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the period of incapacity for work began before the time when his wife died or within the prescribed period after that time`
           AND (`the day` ABOVE `the day on which his wife died`)
           AND (`the number of the day in the period of incapacity for work, counting the first day as 1` ABOVE 196)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for any day of incapacity for work which (a) ... and (b) ..."
    OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A man to whom this section applies who is not entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under subsection (2) above, but who is terminally ill, is entitled"

-- (4) The weekly rate of incapacity benefit payable under this section is that which would apply if he were
-- entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under s 30A.
-- src:1208 | (4) The weekly rate of incapacity benefit payable under this section is that which would apply if he were entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under section 30A above.
@ref s 41(4) (src:1208)
GIVEN `s 30B(6) the weekly rate of long-term incapacity benefit` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 41(4) the weekly rate of incapacity benefit payable under this section` MEANS
    `s 30B(6) the weekly rate of long-term incapacity benefit`     -- NOTHING when the Schedule 4 figure is absent: NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Schedule 4 is omitted from this text

-- (5) A man is not entitled to incapacity benefit under this section if he is over pensionable age; but if he
-- has attained pensionable age, and the period of incapacity for work mentioned in (2)(a) or (3)(a) did not
-- terminate before he attained that age, (a) he shall, if not otherwise entitled to a Category A retirement
-- pension and also not entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of his wife,
-- be entitled to a Category A retirement pension; and (b) the weekly rate of the Category A retirement pension
-- to which he is entitled shall be determined in the prescribed manner.
-- src:1209 | (5) A man is not entitled to incapacity benefit under this section if he is over pensionable age; but if he has attained pensionable age, and the period of incapacity for work mentioned in subsection (2)(a) or (3)(a) above did not terminate before he attained that age—
@ref s 41(5) (src:1209)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `the man` IS A Person
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(5) the man is entitled to incapacity benefit under this section on the day` MEANS
    IF `the day` AT LEAST (`the man`'s `date of attaining pensionable age`)
    THEN JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A man is not entitled to incapacity benefit under this section if he is over pensionable age"
    ELSE NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says only when he is not entitled

-- src:1210 | (a) he shall, if not otherwise entitled to a Category A retirement pension and also not entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of his wife, be entitled to a Category A retirement pension; and
@ref s 41(5) (src:1210)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `the man` IS A Person
      `the period of incapacity for work mentioned in subsection (2)(a) or (3)(a) did not terminate before he attained pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he is entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of his wife` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(5)(a) the man is entitled to a Category A retirement pension` MEANS
    IF (`the day` AT LEAST (`the man`'s `date of attaining pensionable age`))
       AND `the period of incapacity for work mentioned in subsection (2)(a) or (3)(a) did not terminate before he attained pensionable age`
       AND (NOT `he is entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of his wife`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if he has attained pensionable age, and the period of incapacity for work ... did not terminate before he attained that age"; he is entitled if not otherwise entitled to Category A and also not entitled to Category B by his wife's contributions

-- src:1211 | (b) the weekly rate of the Category A retirement pension to which he is entitled (whether by virtue of paragraph (a) above or otherwise) shall be determined in the prescribed manner.
@ref s 41(5) (src:1211)
GIVEN `the weekly rate of the Category A retirement pension determined in the prescribed manner in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 41(5)(b) the weekly rate of the Category A retirement pension in pounds` MEANS
    `the weekly rate of the Category A retirement pension determined in the prescribed manner in pounds`     -- NOTHING when not supplied: NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "determined in the prescribed manner"

-- (6) Where a man entitled to short-term incapacity benefit under (3) attains pensionable age and defers his
-- entitlement to a Category A pension or makes an election under s 54(1), the days of incapacity for work in the
-- period mentioned in (3) are treated, for determining any subsequent entitlement to incapacity benefit under
-- s 30A or its rate, as days of entitlement to short-term incapacity benefit.
-- src:1212 | (6) Where a man entitled to short-term incapacity benefit under subsection (3) above attains pensionable age and defers his entitlement to a Category A pension or makes an election under section 54(1) below, the days of incapacity for work falling within the period of incapacity for work mentioned in that subsection shall, for the purpose of determining any subsequent entitlement to incapacity benefit under section 30A above or the rate of that benefit, be treated as if they had been days of entitlement to short-term incapacity benefit.
@ref s 41(6) (src:1212)
GIVEN `he was entitled to short-term incapacity benefit under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he attains pensionable age and defers his entitlement to a Category A pension or makes an election under section 54(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days of incapacity for work falling within the period of incapacity for work mentioned in subsection (3)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 41(6) the number of days treated as days of entitlement to short-term incapacity benefit` MEANS
    IF `he was entitled to short-term incapacity benefit under subsection (3)` AND `he attains pensionable age and defers his entitlement to a Category A pension or makes an election under section 54(1)`
    THEN JUST `the number of days of incapacity for work falling within the period of incapacity for work mentioned in subsection (3)`
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a man entitled to short-term incapacity benefit under subsection (3) above attains pensionable age and defers ..."

-- (7) References to short-term incapacity benefit at the higher rate include short-term incapacity benefit
-- payable under (3).
-- src:1213 | (7) References to short-term incapacity benefit at the higher rate shall be construed as including short-term incapacity benefit payable under subsection (3) above.
@ref s 41(7) (src:1213)
GIVEN `the benefit is short-term incapacity benefit payable under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 41(7) the short-term incapacity benefit is at the higher rate` MEANS
    IF `the benefit is short-term incapacity benefit payable under subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "shall be construed as including" does not say that other benefit is not at the higher rate

§§ `s 42 Entitlement under s. 40 or 41 after period of employment or training for work`

-- (1A) A person satisfies the relevant tax credit conditions on a day if (a) he is entitled for the day to the
-- disability element of working tax credit (on a claim made by him or jointly) or would be so entitled but for
-- the relevant income, and (b) either working tax credit or any element of child tax credit other than the
-- family element is paid in respect of the day on such a claim.
-- src:1220 | (1A) A person satisfies the relevant tax credit conditions on a day if—
-- src:1221 | (a) he is entitled for the day to the disability element of working tax credit (on a claim made by him or by him jointly with another) or would be so entitled but for the fact that the relevant income (within the meaning of Part 1 of the Tax Credits Act 2002) in his or their case is such that he is not so entitled, and
-- src:1222 | (b) either working tax credit or any element of child tax credit other than the family element is paid in respect of the day on such a claim.
@ref s 42(1A) (src:1220-1222)
GIVEN `the person is entitled for the day to the disability element of working tax credit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person would be so entitled but for the relevant income in their or their joint case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `working tax credit or an element of child tax credit other than the family element is paid in respect of the day on such a claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 42(1A) the person satisfies the relevant tax credit conditions on the day` MEANS
    IF (`the person is entitled for the day to the disability element of working tax credit` OR `the person would be so entitled but for the relevant income in their or their joint case`)
       AND `working tax credit or an element of child tax credit other than the family element is paid in respect of the day on such a claim`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person satisfies the relevant tax credit conditions on a day if—"

-- (1) A person who claims incapacity benefit under s 40 or 41 for a period commencing after ceasing to be in
-- qualifying remunerative work, and (a) the day following was a day of incapacity for work, (b) was entitled to
-- incapacity benefit under that section within the 2 years ending with that day of incapacity for work, and (c)
-- satisfied the relevant tax credit conditions on the day before ceasing: every day during that period (the
-- period of the claim) on which the person satisfied those conditions is treated, for the claim, as a day of
-- incapacity for work. The 2 years ending with a day begin the day after the same day and month two years
-- earlier (fork F10 in NOTES.md; the s 30C(5) rule).
-- src:1215 | (1) Where a person claims incapacity benefit under section 40 or 41 above for a period commencing after he has ceased to be in qualifying remunerative work (within the meaning of Part 1 of the Tax Credits Act 2002) and—
-- src:1216 | (a) the day following that on which he so ceased was a day of incapacity for work for him,
-- src:1217 | (b) he has been entitled to incapacity benefit under that section within the period of two years ending with that day of incapacity for work, and
-- src:1218 | (c) he satisfied the relevant tax credit conditions on the day before he so ceased,
-- src:1219 | every day during that period on which he satisfied those conditions is to be treated for the purposes of the claim as a day of incapacity for work for him.
@ref s 42(1) (src:1215-1219)
GIVEN `the claim is for incapacity benefit under section 40 or 41` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period for which the claim is made` IS A Period
      `the day on which the person ceased to be in qualifying remunerative work` IS A DATE
      `s 30C(1)(a) the day following the day of ceasing was a day of incapacity for work for the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the latest day on or before that day of incapacity for work on which the person was entitled to incapacity benefit under section 40 or 41` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `s 42(1A) the person satisfied the relevant tax credit conditions on the day before ceasing` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the day` IS A DATE
      `s 42(1A) the person satisfies the relevant tax credit conditions on the day` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 42(1) the day is treated as a day of incapacity for work for the claim` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 30A(2)(b) the same day and month a number of whole years from the date` (`the day on which the person ceased to be in qualifying remunerative work` PLUS 1) (0 MINUS 2)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): two years before 29 February in a year with no 29 February
    WHEN JUST twoYearsBefore THEN
        CONSIDER
            `s 30A both`
                (JUST ((`the claim is for incapacity benefit under section 40 or 41`)
                       AND ((`the period for which the claim is made`'s `the first day`) ABOVE `the day on which the person ceased to be in qualifying remunerative work`)
                       AND (`the day` AT LEAST (`the period for which the claim is made`'s `the first day`))
                       AND (`the day` AT MOST (`the period for which the claim is made`'s `the last day`))))
                (`s 30A both`
                    `s 30C(1)(a) the day following the day of ceasing was a day of incapacity for work for the person`
                    (`s 30A both`
                        (CONSIDER `the latest day on or before that day of incapacity for work on which the person was entitled to incapacity benefit under section 40 or 41`
                         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                         WHEN JUST entitled THEN JUST ((entitled ABOVE twoYearsBefore) AND (entitled AT MOST (`the day on which the person ceased to be in qualifying remunerative work` PLUS 1))))
                        (`s 30A both`
                            `s 42(1A) the person satisfied the relevant tax credit conditions on the day before ceasing`
                            `s 42(1A) the person satisfies the relevant tax credit conditions on the day`)))
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every day during that period on which he satisfied those conditions is to be treated" where (a), (b) and (c) hold

-- Seam S23: ssc4 s 93 asks whether the person is entitled to long-term incapacity benefit "by virtue of ...
-- section 42". Section 42 does not itself grant the benefit: it treats days as days of incapacity, and the
-- entitlement under s 40 or 41 then follows if its other conditions are met.
-- src:1215 | (1) Where a person claims incapacity benefit under section 40 or 41 above for a period commencing after he has ceased to be in qualifying remunerative work (within the meaning of Part 1 of the Tax Credits Act 2002) and—
-- src:1216 | (a) the day following that on which he so ceased was a day of incapacity for work for him,
-- src:1217 | (b) he has been entitled to incapacity benefit under that section within the period of two years ending with that day of incapacity for work, and
-- src:1218 | (c) he satisfied the relevant tax credit conditions on the day before he so ceased,
-- src:1219 | every day during that period on which he satisfied those conditions is to be treated for the purposes of the claim as a day of incapacity for work for him.
@ref s 42(1) (src:1215-1219)
GIVEN `s 42(1) the day is treated as a day of incapacity for work for the claim` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is otherwise entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under section 40 or 41 on that footing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 42 the person is entitled to long-term incapacity benefit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 42(1) the day is treated as a day of incapacity for work for the claim`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the person is otherwise entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under section 40 or 41 on that footing` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection treats days as days of incapacity; the other conditions of entitlement are those of s 40 or 41
    OTHERWISE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the person is entitled by virtue of s 42 only through days it treats as days of incapacity

-- (2) "training for work" means training in pursuance of arrangements made under s 2(1) of the Employment and
-- Training Act 1973 or s 2(3) of the Enterprise and New Towns (Scotland) Act 1990, or training of such other
-- description as may be prescribed.
-- src:1228 | In this subsection “training for work” means training for work in pursuance of arrangements made under section 2(1) of the Employment and Training Act 1973 or section 2(3) of the Enterprise and New Towns (Scotland) Act 1990 or training of such other description as may be prescribed.
@ref s 42(2) (src:1228)
GIVEN `the training is in pursuance of arrangements made under section 2(1) of the Employment and Training Act 1973 or section 2(3) of the Enterprise and New Towns (Scotland) Act 1990` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the training is of a description the regulations prescribe` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 42(2) the training is training for work` MEANS
    IF `the training is in pursuance of arrangements made under section 2(1) of the Employment and Training Act 1973 or section 2(3) of the Enterprise and New Towns (Scotland) Act 1990` OR `the training is of a description the regulations prescribe`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this subsection “training for work” means training in pursuance of arrangements made under ..."

-- (2) A person who becomes engaged in training for work, was entitled to incapacity benefit under s 40 or 41
-- for one or more of the 56 days immediately before, and the first day after ceasing to be so engaged is a day of
-- incapacity for work and falls not later than the end of the period of 2 years beginning with the last day for
-- which they were entitled: any day since that day in which they were engaged in training for work is treated,
-- for any claim under that section for a period commencing after they cease, as a day of incapacity for work.
-- "That day" is read as in s 30C(6) (forks F7 and F10 in NOTES.md).
-- src:1223 | (2) Where—
-- src:1224 | (a) a person becomes engaged in training for work, and
-- src:1225 | (b) he was entitled to incapacity benefit under section 40 or 41 above for one or more of the 56 days immediately before he became so engaged, and
-- src:1226 | (c) the first day after he ceases to be so engaged is for him a day of incapacity for work and falls not later than the end of the period of two years beginning with the last day for which he was entitled to incapacity benefit under that section,
-- src:1227 | any day since that day in which he was engaged in training for work shall be treated for the purposes of any claim for incapacity benefit under that section for a period commencing after he ceases to be so engaged as having been a day of incapacity for work.
@ref s 42(2) (src:1223-1227)
GIVEN `the first day on which the person was engaged in training for work` IS A DATE
      `the last day on which the person was entitled to incapacity benefit under section 40 or 41` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the first day after the person ceased to be engaged in training for work` IS A DATE
      `that first day is a day of incapacity for work for the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the training day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 42(2) the training day is treated as a day of incapacity for work` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day on which the person was entitled to incapacity benefit under section 40 or 41`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph needs a last day of entitlement
    WHEN JUST lastDay THEN
        CONSIDER `s 30A(2)(b) the same day and month a number of whole years from the date` lastDay 2
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): two years from 29 February in a year with no 29 February
        WHEN JUST twoYearsOn THEN
            IF (lastDay AT LEAST (`the first day on which the person was engaged in training for work` MINUS 56))
               AND (lastDay BELOW `the first day on which the person was engaged in training for work`)
               AND `that first day is a day of incapacity for work for the person`
               AND (`the first day after the person ceased to be engaged in training for work` BELOW twoYearsOn)
               AND (`the training day` ABOVE lastDay)
               AND (`the training day` AT LEAST `the first day on which the person was engaged in training for work`)
               AND (`the training day` BELOW `the first day after the person ceased to be engaged in training for work`)
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any day since that day in which he was engaged in training for work" where (a), (b) and (c) hold

-- (3) For the purposes of s 42 "week" means any period of 7 days.
-- src:1229 | (3) For the purposes of this section “week” means any period of 7 days.
@ref s 42(3) (src:1229)
`s 42(3) the number of days in a week` MEANS 7
